/; EXPECT_ERROR: SpawnRequiresUserFunction
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/; REGRESSION: `spawn println(...)` used to CRASH the compiler (SIGSEGV).
/;
/; A built-in is emitted inline rather than called through a symbol, so no
/; function for it exists in the module. IRGen looked one up, got null, and
/; dereferenced it. The assert that was supposed to catch this is compiled out
/; in Release builds, so the user saw a bare segfault with no message.
/;
/; `println` is also variadic, which breaks the second assumption: its declared
/; parameter list is shorter than the call's argument list, so copying the
/; arguments by parameter index walked off the end of the vector.
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

spawn println("hello")
